            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What did studēre originally mean? (\"To be eager / apply oneself.\") Its English cousins? (Student, studio, studious.) Say \"I study\" — and notice it uses the same -o as hablo and trabajo. (Estudio.) Next: put a verb and a noun together into your first real sentence."
            }
